      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1378559842,
      "text": "Myrica gale is a species of flowering plant in the family Myricaceae native to cool temperate regions of Eurasia and North America. Common names include bog-myrtle, sweet gale, Dutch myrtle, and sweetgale."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Myrica gale",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myrica_gale",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 171581394,
      "text": "Mirto de Brabante o mirto de turbera es una especie vegetal, perteneciente a la familia de las miricáceas."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Myrica gale",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myrica_gale",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 228092274,
      "text": "Le piment royal (Myrica gale), myrte des marais, myrte du brabant ou pour les francophones d'Amérique le bois-sent-bon ou myrique baumier est une plante arbustive de la famille des Myricaceae."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Myrica gale",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myrica_gale",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 68030109,
      "text": "Myrica gale, comummente conhecida como samouco-do-brabante, é uma espécie de planta com flor, pertencente à família das Miricáceas e ao tipo fisionómico dos fanerófitos."
    }
